response:
 We can calculate the area of the semicircles constructed along the legs and hypotenuse of the right triangle. The radius of the semicircle along a leg $$a$$ is $$\frac{a}{2}$$, and the radius of the semicircle along the hypotenuse $$h$$ is $$\frac{h}{2}$$. 

Let's calculate the area of the semicircle along the leg with length 6 inches:

\begin{align*}
\textcolor{green}{\text{[arc radius]}} &= \frac{6}{2} = 3 \text{ inches} \\
\textcolor{blue}{\text{[arc area]}} &= \frac{1}{2}\pi r^2 = \frac{1}{2}\pi\left( 3 \right)^2 = \frac{9}{2}\pi \text{ square inches}
\end{align*}

Similarly, we can calculate the area of the semicircle along the leg with length 8 inches:

\begin{align*}
\textcolor{green}{\text{[arc radius]}} &= \frac{8}{2} = 4 \text{ inches} \\
\textcolor{blue}{\text{[arc area]}} &= \frac{1}{2}\pi r^2 = \frac{1}{2}\pi\left( 4 \right)^2 = 8\pi \text{ square inches}
\end{align*}

Now, let's calculate the area of the semicircle along the hypotenuse. First, we need to find the length of the hypotenuse using the Pythagorean theorem:

\begin{align*}
a^2 + b^2 &= c^2 \\
6^2 + 8^2 &= c^2 \\
36 + 64 &= c^2 \\
100 &= c^2 \\
c &= 10 \text{ inches}
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
\textcolor{green}{\text{[arc radius]}} &= \frac{10}{2} = 5 \text{ inches} \\
\textcolor{blue}{\text{[arc area]}} &= \frac{1}{2}\pi r^2 = \frac{1}{2}\pi\left( 5 \right)^2 = \frac{25}{2}\pi \text{ square inches}
\end{align*}

The area of the right triangle is calculated by the formula:

\begin{align*}
\text{Area}_{\triangle} &= \frac{1}{2}\times\text{base}\times\text{height} \\
&= \frac{1}{2}\times6\times8 \\
&= 24 \text{ square inches}
\end{align*}

The total area of the two crescents is the sum of the areas of the semicircles minus the area of the right triangle:

\begin{align*}
\textcolor{blue}{\text{[crescent areas]}} &= \left( \frac{9}{2}\pi + 8\pi + \frac{25}{2}\pi \right) - 24 \\
&= \left( \frac{9 + 16 + 25}{2}\pi \right) - 24 \\
&= \left( \frac{50}{2}\pi \right) - 24 \\
&= 25\pi - 24 \text{ square inches}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the total area of the two non-shaded crescent-shaped regions is $$\boxed{25\pi - 24}$$ square inches.

